    {
      "number": 26,
      "animations": [],
      "text": "ConclusionLinear Independence: Equivalent to N(A) = 0, tested by placing vectors ascolumns of A and checking for free variables.Spanning: Extends the definition of column space C(A) as all linearcombinations of columns.Basis: Combines independence and spanning. For R^n, checking if n vectorsform a basis is equivalent to testing matrix invertibility.Dimension: Bridges matrix rank r to geometry: dim(C(A)) = r and dim(N(A)) =n - r.",
